CORE
JmlConjunction
--function JmlConjunction.product --jml-source src/main/java/JmlConjunction.java --unwind 5 -cp target/classes
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR
^.*FAILURE$
--
Regression for JML compound boolean logic in postconditions.

Verifies the JML pipeline correctly:
- Parses && (AND), || (OR), ==> (IMPLIES) operators
- Resolves multiple parameters in a single expression
- Lowers (a && b) ==> c into !(a && b) || c
- Combines multiple ensures clauses

The product method takes non-negative x, y and the contract
encodes both branches: (x>0 && y>0 → result>0) and
(x==0 || y==0 → result==0).
